# Files that are executed or parsed by Linux tooling on the server.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks these out with CRLF, which turns
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash` into `#!/usr/bin/env bash^M` and fails on the server with
# "bad interpreter". These are installed directly by rsync/cp, so the working
# tree -- not just the repository blob -- has to stay LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
